== Incremental Writing & Resume ==
Write test-report.md incrementally — create the file with the header and empty results table
first, then update it after each AC item is tested. Do not wait until all items are done.

Before starting, check if test-report.md already exists. A previous session may have been
interrupted mid-testing. If it exists, read it:
- AC items with PASS/FAIL status and evidence → already tested, skip them
- AC items with no status or marked SKIP without evidence → test these
- A file with only headers or an empty table means resume from the first AC item
- If Verdict is already filled → testing is complete, verify consistency and finish
Do NOT assume an existing file means testing is done — check which AC items have results.

== Workflow (strict order) ==
1. Read acceptance criteria — list every AC item
2. Create test-report.md with header and empty results table
3. Run: ${FOURX_BIN:-4x} verify {{.Feature.ID}}
4. Read the generated verify.json for command results
5. For each AC item, collect evidence and update test-report.md immediately
6. Update the Summary and Verdict sections
7. If verify.json passed is true, write final-report.md

